WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.648
Network services are the part
organizations most often defer,

2
00:00:04.648 --> 00:00:08.450
because DNS, DHCP and address
management still work.

3
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.588
That's exactly how they keep
the old directory alive.

4
00:00:11.588 --> 00:00:13.526
The three form one surface.

5
00:00:13.526 --> 00:00:17.687
DNS usually lives in zones
integrated with Active Directory,

6
00:00:17.687 --> 00:00:21.767
so every domain controller sits
in the name-resolution path,

7
00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:25.113
and Active Directory can't
retire until DNS moves.

8
00:00:25.113 --> 00:00:29.701
DHCP servers are authorized in the
forest, but that check is Windows

9
00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:34.863
policing itself: it stops an unauthorized
Windows server, not a rogue device.

10
00:00:34.863 --> 00:00:37.883
And address management,
in many organizations,

11
00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:40.362
is a spreadsheet one person maintains.

12
00:00:40.362 --> 00:00:43.662
Without it, DNS and DHCP drift.

13
00:00:43.662 --> 00:00:45.738
So the program moves them together.

14
00:00:45.738 --> 00:00:50.307
One governed IPAM authority
covers the whole address surface,

15
00:00:50.307 --> 00:00:54.962
on-premises and cloud, and DNS and
DHCP derive their records from it.

16
00:00:54.962 --> 00:00:59.862
Disagreement between them is drift,
and there's no DNS-only run.

17
00:00:59.862 --> 00:01:06.181
Federal controls point the same
way: SP 800-53 treats secure name

18
00:01:06.181 --> 00:01:10.149
resolution and the component
inventory as controls of their own.

19
00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:13.767
The common failure is to
modernize identity and policy

20
00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.913
and leave these for a Phase
2 that rarely happens.

21
00:01:16.913 --> 00:01:20.874
A forest that still hosts
DNS has not been retired.

22
00:01:20.874 --> 00:01:25.924
That makes it a scope and funding
decision for the sponsor and the CIO:

23
00:01:25.924 --> 00:01:31.238
put DNS, DHCP and IPAM in the core
program now, with one IPAM authority.

24
00:01:31.238 --> 00:01:34.200
The pilot division's
zones move in Phase 2.
